    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that makes sense. i also need to show the accumulated depreciation for the end of year 3 for the audit trail. could you show me how that looks? and just to be sure, is there anything else i should keep in mind regarding how the value drops each year?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the end of year 3, you simply multiply the annual depreciation expense by three years. Since your annual depreciation is $\\$5,000$, the accumulated depreciation after three years would be $\\$15,000$. It's important to remember that the book value decreases consistently each year, which is the *straight-line* method's defining characteristic. Unlike some other methods, the depreciation expense is the same every year, not a fluctuating amount.",
      "source": "target",
